## Dynamic Workflow Governance

<!-- REQUIRED: Keep in sync with runtime-capabilities.workflow_governance. -->

- **Availability:** Use only when `workflow_governance.status == "available"`.
- **Recurring scripts:** Save recurring workflows only as reviewed scripts under `.claude/workflows/` after a bounded successful run.
- **Slice-first cost probe:** Run a narrow path or question before broad repository workflows.
- **Governance no-write rule:** Workflow agents must not write project-governance artifacts such as `docs/planning/**`, `.vibeos/**`, `.claude/settings*.json`, or saved workflow scripts unless the active Work Order explicitly scopes that write and a review accepts it.
- **Evidence:** Capture workflow prompt, saved script path when any, phase/agent counts, token evidence, findings, and comparison against the non-workflow baseline.
- **Disable path:** Turn workflows off through `/config`, `disableWorkflows`, managed settings, or `CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_WORKFLOWS=1`.

## Adoption Status

<!-- ADAPT: Planned | Bounded Slice | Adopted | Rejected | Disabled -->

Dynamic workflows are not default until a bounded slice produces evidence and an adoption verdict.

